From d927babe27d76bd3b9fe6dbf9977b45017b067eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:23:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add D8 LlmClient abstraction with D11 bounded-retry
 fail-closed loop

Day 6 backend work, no dependency on physical Fire TV hardware, Android
toolchain, or the current P2 emulator blocker.

- backend/ai/client/base.py: abstract LlmClient with the D11 contract
  implemented once, shared by every provider: strict-schema structured
  calls, bounded retry (2), fail-closed on exhaustion. A provider subclass
  only implements "ask the model once" -- retry/validate/fail-closed logic
  cannot be duplicated or forgotten per provider.
- backend/ai/client/anthropic_client.py: the locked D8 provider, using
  tool-use to force schema-shaped output. Reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the
  environment only (D25/PRIV-1640); refuses to construct without one
  (LlmNotConfiguredError) rather than degrading silently. anthropic SDK is
  imported lazily so it is not required to run the test suite.
- backend/ai/client/operations.py: named AI operations mapped to exactly
  one regime (SAFE-900) and one task-appropriate model (D8) -- sonnet-5 for
  document structuring (accuracy-critical, feeds D16 confirmation review),
  haiku-4-5 for narrower/latency-sensitive transforms and sequencing.
- backend/ai/client/results.py: StructuredCallResult + to_audit_log_entry(),
  whose return type is structurally incapable of carrying prompt/response
  content (PRIV-1652) -- the projection has no such field to leak.
- backend/ai/client/fake_client.py: deterministic test double (used only by
  backend/tests/test_llm_client.py); no network or API key needed to test
  this module.
- backend/requirements.txt: + jsonschema (D11 server-side validation),
  + anthropic (D8, lazily imported).

Verification: 42/42 backend tests pass (24 pre-existing + 18 new), including
with the `anthropic` package NOT installed, confirming the lazy-import
isolation holds. No secrets, no clinical content, no unrelated files
touched. This does not implement ASSIST or GUIDE application logic (D12/D13)
-- those remain separate, later modules per the locked "no shared ai.call()
helper" rule; this is the shared transport layer only. P1 physical
validation and P2 remain untouched and PENDING.

